From d5e7156bca61442b221a0d57429e4a4c71b38154 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:06:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] lifecycle guard: peel command wrappers before
 classifying a nested login shell

`_nested_shell_input(view)` checked su/runuser/doas/sudo only in the first
command word, then peeled every transparent wrapper at once (su and sudo
included). So `env su -l bob < f`, `nice su -l bob`, `timeout 5 su -l bob`,
`exec su -l bob`, `command su -l bob` and `sudo su - bob` landed on `bob` or
nothing and were never classified as a login shell: the stdin file, here-string,
heredoc or piped file that shell parses was not walked in nested scope (where
alias names are unknown). The lifecycle guard allowed `t ( bash <live
kanban.db> )` fed that way under every session alias set, None included
(fail-open; t_d57454ce9f63e6f0, found reviewing PR #3081).

Five whys:
1. Why allowed? The nested-scope walk never saw f: `_nested_shell_input`
   returned None for `env su -l bob`.
2. Why None? The su/runuser/doas/sudo launcher checks ran only at the first
   command word (`env`).
3. Why not after peeling? Peeling was all-at-once via
   `_peel_transparent_prefixes`, which also peels su/sudo themselves, so the
   launcher was skipped, never inspected.
4. Why all-at-once? The function predates the launcher cases; they were added
   in front of it rather than inside the wrapper walk.
5. Why not caught? Tests only covered bare launchers.

Fix: walk the wrapper chain one wrapper at a time
(`_peel_transparent_prefixes(..., limit=1)`, a new optional bound), classifying
each position as a launcher (su/runuser/doas/sudo shell modes) before peeling
it. `exec -l` anywhere in the chain stays sticky (fails closed). The final
command keeps the old ssh / shell / BASH_ENV logic. Every caller (stdin
redirect, heredoc owner, compound-command redirections, piped/fed files) goes
through `_nested_shell_input`, so all shapes are covered.

Proof: tests/cron/test_lifecycle_guard_session_aliases.py
- RED on the parent: 21 new `test_nested_login_shell_body_treats_names_as_unknown`
  shapes (env/exec/command/nice/timeout su -l bob < f, sudo su -l bob < f,
  env sudo -i < f, nice doas -s < f, command runuser -l bob < f,
  { env su -l bob; } < f, cat f | env/exec/command/nice/timeout 5 su -l bob,
  heredoc/here-string/-c variants) plus `test_nested_shell_input_shapes`
  failed; GREEN after the fix (353 passed).
- Controls stay allowed under {zz}: `env cat < f`, `nice cat < f`,
  `timeout 5 cat < f`, `cat f | env cat`, `env su -l bob -c true < f`,
  `nice su -l bob -c true <<< T`, `sudo cat < f`,
  `env runuser -u bob -- cat < f`.
- All 37 test files referencing the lifecycle guard: 2827 passed.
